  {
   "text": "Figure 8. (a) One backward step: the times at which a traveller can safely arrive over a road are shifted back by the travel\ntime, and the times when fire is on the road are removed, leaving the safe start times (two windows with a gap). (b) The solver\nreturns an answer with a certificate, which an independent checker that shares no code with the solver accepts or rejects.\nTests: 0 disagreements with brute force on 12,000 random networks; 5 of 5 planted bugs caught (3,000 networks per family);\nall 174 village certificates of the worked examples pass the checker. Source: research/kcf-theorem, product/wfg-roadlayer.",
